course: dictionary
lesson: 10594
title: The underside
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The underside is the bottom side of something, the part that faces down. Look at the word in two pieces: under and side. Under means below, and side means a surface or edge, so underside is the surface below. «The underside of a leaf has tiny holes called stomata» means the part of the leaf that faces down, not the top that faces the sun.
explain: Words in a sentence give clues. «Owl butterflies have large eye spots on the underside of their wings» tells you the eye spots are on the part of the wings you see when they are closed or flat, facing down. Try the swap check: put the bottom side or the part facing down in place of underside, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The underside is a noun, so it names a thing, and it can be plural: undersides. You will often see it in phrases such as «on the underside» and «the underside of». Scientists look at the underside of a leaf or a rock, and everyday things like tables, cars and boats have undersides too.
fact: Underside means the bottom side or surface of something, the part facing down.
fact: «Underside» is a noun, and its plural is «undersides».
fact: «The underside of a leaf» is where tiny holes called stomata are, and they let air in and water vapour out.
fact: «Leaves lose water vapour through tiny holes called stomata, mostly on the underside.»
fact: «The blue morpho butterfly» has a brown underside with eye spots that can make it seem to vanish when it closes its wings.
exercise: «The underside of a leaf has tiny holes called stomata.» What is the underside of a leaf? | *The part facing down | The bright green edge | The stalk that joins it to the tree | The top, where the sun shines
exercise: In science lessons, minibeasts often hide on the underside of what? | *A rock | A cloud | A bright lamp | A glass of cold water
exercise: Owl butterflies have large eye spots on the underside of their wings. Find and copy the word that means the part facing down. | owl | wings | butterflies | *underside
test: «The moth rested with its wings closed, showing the underside.» What does underside mean here? | *The bottom side, the part facing down | The top side that faces the sky | The part where the moth eats | The very end of the wings
test: What is the plural of underside? | undersided | undersides' | *undersides | underside's
exam: Which sentence uses underside correctly? | Undersides ran across the field very quickly. | The underside is a loud, happy song. | *Mum painted the underside of the table green. | She underside the ball over the net.
